WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.269 --> 00:00:08.730
Netflix, Amazon, Hulu, a theater near you—the
modern film fan has more choices than ever.

00:00:08.730 --> 00:00:11.940
To help you sort through them all, we've taken
a hard look at this year's most critically

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:16.039
acclaimed features and assembled a list of
best bets. Here are some standouts of what

00:00:16.039 --> 00:00:19.760
Hollywood had to offer in the first half of
2016.

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:21.500
Captain America: Civil War

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:25.880
Captain America: Civil War rounded up a hefty
assortment of Marvel Cinematic Universe favorites—and

00:00:25.880 --> 00:00:30.449
some highly anticipated new faces. The result
is a thrilling, action-packed adventure of

00:00:30.449 --> 00:00:35.079
superhero spectacle that even the most anti-comic
book film fan might enjoy.

00:00:35.079 --> 00:00:35.679
The Witch

00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:43.700
"Boo! There you are… Boo!"

00:00:46.410 --> 00:00:49.730
It's hard to find a horror movie with enough
faith in its audience to take things slow

00:00:49.730 --> 00:00:54.430
and get weird. The Witch, which unspools in
a spooky thicket of woods in 17th-century

00:00:54.430 --> 00:00:59.149
New England, follows a familiar path. But
it's director Robert Eggers' flair for imagery

00:00:59.149 --> 00:01:01.309
that makes The Witch so creepily compelling.

00:01:01.309 --> 00:01:02.770
10 Cloverfield Lane

00:01:02.770 --> 00:01:08.229
10 Cloverfield Lane uses 2008's Cloverfield
as the launchpad for the story of a woman,

00:01:08.229 --> 00:01:13.020
played by Mary Elizabeth Winstead, who flees
a busted engagement only to run into disaster.

00:01:13.020 --> 00:01:17.389
She ends up locked in an underground shelter
by a man, played by an unhinged John Goodman,

00:01:17.389 --> 00:01:21.549
who insists the Earth is under attack. Is
he a hero, or a psycho killer?

00:01:21.549 --> 00:01:22.880
The Nice Guys

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:26.709
Writer-director Shane Black is the king of
the action comedy, getting his start by writing

00:01:26.709 --> 00:01:28.729
the original Lethal Weapon back in 1987.

00:01:28.729 --> 00:01:32.079
"Do you really wanna jump? Do you wanna?"

00:01:32.079 --> 00:01:36.039
The Nice Guys, a lower-key buddy cop comedy
starring Ryan Gosling and Russell Crowe as

00:01:36.039 --> 00:01:40.950
partners in '70s L.A., proves that Black is
back, and he hasn’t lost his gifts.

00:01:40.950 --> 00:01:42.399
Green Room

00:01:42.399 --> 00:01:46.380
Viewers are plunged into the hellish ordeal
experienced by a punk band who attract the

00:01:46.380 --> 00:01:50.799
bloodthirsty ire of some murderous neo-Nazi
skinheads. Did we mention that Patrick Stewart

00:01:50.799 --> 00:01:53.770
is the homicidal owner of the club where the
band is trapped?

00:01:53.770 --> 00:01:57.169
Starring the late Anton Yelchin, Green Room
is equal parts smart and nasty—and one of

00:01:57.169 --> 00:02:00.270
the more sinfully enjoyable indie efforts
of 2016.

00:02:00.270 --> 00:02:01.659
Hail, Caesar!

00:02:01.659 --> 00:02:06.029
Hail, Caesar!, which stars Josh Brolin as
a studio fixer in Hollywood’s golden age

00:02:06.029 --> 00:02:09.680
on a mission to solve the disappearance of
a dopey movie star, played by George Clooney,

00:02:09.680 --> 00:02:13.530
who's been drugged and abducted from the set.
Assembled with the typical Coen Brothers quirk,

00:02:13.530 --> 00:02:16.470
it’s some of the most fun we’ve had at
the movies this year.

00:02:16.470 --> 00:02:18.480
Everybody Wants Some!!

00:02:20.460 --> 00:02:21.800
"You cool, man?"

00:02:21.810 --> 00:02:26.310
With his 1993 cult classic Dazed and Confused,
Richard Linklater assembled an insightful

00:02:26.310 --> 00:02:30.600
look at high school in the ‘70s. He picked
that thread back up with Everybody Wants Some!!

00:02:30.600 --> 00:02:34.780
It offers a look at college life and packs
in a killer, era-appropriate soundtrack featuring

00:02:34.780 --> 00:02:37.950
classic hits from Cheap Trick and Van Halen.

00:02:37.950 --> 00:02:39.250
Deadpool

00:02:39.250 --> 00:02:43.390
How do you make a Deadpool movie that embraces
the character's filthy comics persona while

00:02:43.390 --> 00:02:47.370
still being broad enough money to prop up
a franchise? We still can't quite believe

00:02:47.370 --> 00:02:51.790
they pulled it off, but Fox made it work.
The anti-hero, played by Ryan Reynolds, slashes

00:02:51.790 --> 00:02:55.610
up bad guys and breaks the fourth wall with
equal abandon.

00:02:55.610 --> 00:02:57.170
Midnight Special

00:02:57.170 --> 00:03:01.540
Director Jeff Nichols and actor Michael Shannon
perfectly captured modern-day, middle-class

00:03:01.540 --> 00:03:07.610
dread in 2011's Take Shelter. The pair reunited
in 2016 for Midnight Special, a movie about

00:03:07.610 --> 00:03:12.030
a father racing to protect his son from outside
forces bent on taking advantage of his seemingly

00:03:12.030 --> 00:03:13.220
superhuman abilities.

00:03:13.220 --> 00:03:17.200
Thanks for watching! Subscribe to our YouTube
channel to watch more videos like the one

00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:20.860
you just saw. And leave us a comment to let
us know what 2016 movie was your favorite

00:03:20.860 --> 00:03:21.360
so far...

